WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:03.690
So here we have a sample of cobalt. Now I
have got lots and

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.430
lots of different samples of cobalt in my
drawer, so this is

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.720
cobalt sponge.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:16.010
Cobalt is, in many ways, similar to iron.
It can form magnets.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.260
So this cobalt has been generated from a solution
and it’s

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.390
been made in very, very finely dispersed so
it has a very large

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:26.130
surface area. It’s very good for doing catalytic
reactions.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:32.189
The magnets that you use in colour televisions,
for the loud

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:37.770
speakers, contain cobalt. You need to use
cobalt in the

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.610
magnets in the colour television or the old
sort of colour

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:44.650
television not the ones with LCD screens because
the

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:52.270
magnetic fields from larger magnets could
affect the electron

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:55.970
guns and so spoil the colours so you need
a very small

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.540
magnet on your loud speaker or the colours
all go funny.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:02.930
Cobalt sponge absorbs lots and lots of gas
for perhaps

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.509
hydrogenation.

00:01:04.509 --> 00:01:10.329
Many years ago, in the 1970s, when there was
a civil war in

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:15.369
Africa in the region Katanga where cobalt
is mined, there was

00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:18.620
a shortage of cobalt and the production of
colour televisions

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.799
stopped for some considerable time until the
production

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:22.799
restarted.

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:25.940
So you can see it flows in the bottle. So
I have another

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:29.679
sample of cobalt and that is simply a foil.
So again that is a

00:01:29.679 --> 00:01:35.420
very nice malleable tin-type foil; very, very
good structures.

